.\" Begin generated content:
.TH "wob" "1" "2025-05-22"
.PP
.SH "نام (NAME)"
.PP
wob \- Wayland Overlay Bar
.PP
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.PP
wob is a lightweight overlay volume/backlight/progress/anything bar for Wayland.\&
.PP
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.PP
\fBwob\fR [options.\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.PP
\fB-c, --config <file>\fR
.RS 4
Configuration file location.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-v, --verbose\fR
.RS 4
Increase verbosity of messages, defaults to errors and warnings only.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-V, --version\fR
.RS 4
Show the version number and quit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Show help message and quit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH "نحوه استفاده (USAGE)"
.PP
wob reads values to display from standard input in the following formats:
.PP
<value>
.PP
or
.PP
<value> <style>
.PP
Where <value> is number in interval from 0 to \fBmax\fR and <style> is style defined in \fBwob.\&ini\fR(5).\&
.PP
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.PP
wob searches for a config file in the following locations, in this order:
.PP
1.\& $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wob/wob.\&ini
2.\& ~/.\&config/wob/wob.\&ini
3.\& /etc/wob/wob.\&ini
.PP
For information on the config file format, see \fBwob.\&ini\fR(5).\&
.PP
.SH "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
.PP
The following environment variables have an effect on wob:
.PP
\fBWOB_DISABLE_PLEDGE\fR
.RS 4
Disable seccomp syscall filtering on Linux.\& Set this if you are having trouble running wob with tools like valgrind.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.PP
\fBwob.\&ini\fR(5)
